From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lukasz Sobala <lsobala1@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 29 Jul 2026 00:47:09 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] riscv: assemble the T-Head vendor instructions with mainline
 binutils

The RISC-V FSBL is written for T-Head's own toolchain, which knows the C906
vendor CSRs by name and accepts the XTheadCmo cache mnemonics.  Mainline
binutils knows neither, so the build dies with

  Error: unknown CSR `mhcr'
  Error: unrecognized opcode `icache.iall'
  Error: unrecognized opcode `sync.i'

Give the assembler the raw encodings instead.  A CSR operand is parsed as an
ordinary expression, so a plain .set is enough for the four vendor CSRs; the
two cache ops become .long, which is already how this tree spells dcache.ipa,
dcache.cpa, dcache.cipa and sync.s in lib/cpu/riscv/cache.c.  The resulting
object code is identical to what the vendor toolchain emits - verified by
disassembly (csrw 0x7c0 == 0x7c019073, icache.iall == 0x0100000b,
sync.i == 0x01a0000b).

Upstream would rather use .insn or the XTheadCmo extension names, but those
need binutils 2.39+ for XTheadCmo and would still leave the CSRs unnamed, so
this stays the smaller change.
---
diff --git a/lib/cpu/riscv/cache.c b/lib/cpu/riscv/cache.c
index 54828f8..6527dfa 100644
--- a/lib/cpu/riscv/cache.c
+++ b/lib/cpu/riscv/cache.c
@@ -57,14 +57,14 @@ void flush_dcache_range(uintptr_t start, size_t size)
 void enable_dcache(void)
 {
 	asm volatile(
-		"csrs mhcr, %0;" ::"rI"(0x2)
+		"csrs 0x7c1, %0;"  /* mhcr */ ::"rI"(0x2)
 	);
 }
 
 void disable_dcache(void)
 {
 	asm volatile(
-		"csrc mhcr, %0;" ::"rI"(0x2)
+		"csrc 0x7c1, %0;"  /* mhcr */ ::"rI"(0x2)
 	);
 }
 
diff --git a/lib/cpu/riscv/cpu_helper.c b/lib/cpu/riscv/cpu_helper.c
index 7e093fa..9db8677 100644
--- a/lib/cpu/riscv/cpu_helper.c
+++ b/lib/cpu/riscv/cpu_helper.c
@@ -10,9 +10,18 @@
 
 void sync_cache(void)
 {
+	/*
+	 * icache.iall
+	 * | 31 - 25 | 24 - 20 | 19 - 15 | 14 - 12 | 11 - 7 | 6 - 0 |
+	 *   0000000    10000     00000      000      00000  0001011
+	 *
+	 * sync.i
+	 * | 31 - 25 | 24 - 20 | 19 - 15 | 14 - 12 | 11 - 7 | 6 - 0 |
+	 *   0000000    11010     00000      000      00000  0001011
+	 */
 	asm volatile(
-			"icache.iall\n"
-			"sync.i\n"
+			".long 0x0100000b\n"
+			".long 0x01a0000b\n"
 			:
 			:
 			: "memory");
diff --git a/lib/cpu/riscv/csr.h b/lib/cpu/riscv/csr.h
index 6f05d39..6f79772 100644
--- a/lib/cpu/riscv/csr.h
+++ b/lib/cpu/riscv/csr.h
@@ -3,6 +3,19 @@
 #ifndef RISCV_CSR_ENCODING_H
 #define RISCV_CSR_ENCODING_H
 
+/*
+ * T-Head C906 vendor CSRs. Mainline binutils only knows the standard CSR
+ * names, so give the assembler plain symbols to resolve - a CSR operand is
+ * parsed as an ordinary expression, and this produces byte-identical
+ * encodings to the T-Head toolchain.
+ */
+#ifdef __ASSEMBLY__
+.set mxstatus, 0x7c0
+.set mhcr,     0x7c1
+.set mcor,     0x7c2
+.set mhint,    0x7c5
+#endif
+
 #define MSTATUS_UIE         0x00000001
 #define MSTATUS_SIE         0x00000002
 #define MSTATUS_HIE         0x00000004
